score_pct: 67.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading implementation uses unwrap_or_default pattern without distinguishing
    NotFound from parse/permission errors. Reviewer flagged silent env var handling
    but not this specific from_file_or_default issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote CWE-209 checks in exit_codes.rs tests verifying auth error
    messages don''t expose internals. TEA security tests included ''CWE-209: auth
    error messages don''t expose internals'' and ''Config errors don''t leak file
    contents''.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #9: ''tenant field uses raw Option<String> instead of
    TenantId newtype... axiathon-core exports TenantId, but both Cli and SiemClient
    use raw Option<String> for tenant. This bypasses validated constructors at the
    trust boundary.'' TEA also wrote header injection tests for tenant ID.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted the missing keyring dependency but did not
    flag the 6 deps using direct versions instead of workspace references.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #5: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields \u2014\
    \ security-sensitive fields ignored without warning... If an operator puts token\
    \ = \"my-secret\" in cli.toml, serde silently drops it. The operator believes\
    \ their token is configured but it isn't.' Recommended deny_unknown_fields."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #6: 'Two vacuous tests \u2014 assertions never execute...\
    \ config_error_does_not_expose_file_contents... The if let Err(e) branch never\
    \ executes, so the assertion about not exposing secrets never runs. This test\
    \ always passes regardless of behavior. It's a false green.'"
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #6 also covers this: ''config_does_not_load_token_from_file...
    calls has_secret_fields() which is a hardcoded false return. The test asserts
    a constant. It can never fail regardless of what RawConfig does.'' Though the
    specific test_default_config zero-assertion case isn''t called out by name, the
    pattern of vacuous tests was caught.'
